<description>&lt;p&gt;The Colombian government has ordered the temporary militarization of Cúcuta and deployed troops to the Venezuela border city amid rising violence, while President De la Espriella has also ordered a broader military buildup in border areas. Security forces are confronting a wave of crackdowns that include charges against nine former FARC commanders for war crimes and a controversial anti-narcotics operation that has sparked questions over civilian killings. Cuts to the country's human rights court under De la Espriella threaten the institution that oversees such abuses. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxPc1ZSZlJhZnhXbWtIVDhwaTZWeGVLQlo5LVhGZ3kzcnVicUQ5dXVEOFNCWDlZcHR6M2YyV2NVN0pCTGphYy1sTlpLbXp0dXB5ekk0c0p2Z1A5N3AxVTB6dGVxajVKLTJHcGFiVW82a21HenJTdkQzcndRV21uaXc5R1ZTWk9JVlUwU3B2OVlyYVNSakZ3d0JVcWRPY3pzcG94UlJXZGd3?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE94elBoTi0xRmg5bmhPeUZRQi1JcGZfOW9ZRkxjQmI2Mnk1ZWwxVW1PRkxfZ0VzREp5ZW9KMWFOTUZNRUVPcDY0V2ZRTGtXTmdoWDViQy1vRW4?oc=5&quot;&gt;AFP Fact Check&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiaEFVX3lxTE0zNE50Zk0zSVdkRFNrb1lCcmd5eVp0R2hZd3FnaVc4WTc5SFhtbUN1SUxhWXpkR1hwNGVTYjFrLVRocll5TDhicERHX3R3elNiTXBQcjU1dFhLTFpPMFl0TUtIaXRMQzJG?oc=5&quot;&gt;World Socialist Web Site&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiywFBVV95cUxQbzBHSVZtU1pzbk9zQ0dNQUNzNVhsanJJY0RsUERUanI0T1JURkZSWUtWdHRqSW8wanBTRVJtamlUM0lRN0hTZUI1NVB2WW9ocjNKVnF3UXFrZjBsVUJPaFFqWi1NZjRuZ3Z4R1JxNHc0NWJxenBoQ0t2ZGk3bFBwMXJjcFh1QjVId2dJY3lMZlliLXFHUzlEY3Mwdk9XT1JZS3RnUFdNaldqOV9ZeTh0OWFrODNMcTBVZDRaVDB6VUZ